WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.120
An analysis draws a group around some cells.

2
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.120
Is it one type, or two?

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.430
Recall the idea. A real type usually spaces its cells out in its own mosaic.

4
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:20.353
Here is one type. Its cells keep their distance, and its arbors overlap.

5
00:00:21.417 --> 00:00:25.017
The coverage factor is the number of arbors over an average point.

6
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.810
Now pour in a second type, placed independently.

7
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.070
Colour every cell the same.

8
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:37.173
Predict. Treated as one type, what happens to the spacing, and to the coverage?

9
00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.407
The spacing usually turns patchy.

10
00:00:46.027 --> 00:00:49.147
A cell of one type can sit right beside a cell of the other.

11
00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:53.707
And the coverage adds up, so it reads higher than either type's own.

12
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:58.747
So an unusually high coverage can be a sign that two types were merged.

13
00:00:59.717 --> 00:01:02.277
But some real types are only weakly regular.

14
00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:05.737
A mosaic is strong support, not a strict rule.

15
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.670
Each census method tests a different part of the rule.

16
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:15.003
Imaging grouped cells by light response, and found at least 32 types.

17
00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:20.513
RNA sequencing grouped cells by gene expression, and ended with 46.

18
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:26.157
One cluster held two direction-selective types already known from function.

19
00:01:27.157 --> 00:01:28.557
Clustering alone had missed them.

20
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:33.387
Another team recorded spikes and found 42 functional types.

21
00:01:34.187 --> 00:01:37.847
For some cells, they also read that same cell's RNA or shape.

22
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:43.937
There, three sustained ON direction-selective types shared one RNA cluster, called

23
00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:44.937
C10.

24
00:01:45.417 --> 00:01:50.117
Electron microscopy of one small patch supported at least 35 types.

25
00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.827
These are not rival answers.

26
00:01:53.727 --> 00:01:56.567
Each reflects a method, a preparation and a resolution.

27
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.570
The most trustworthy types are the ones that more than one method finds.

28
00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:04.413
A primate needs its own census.

29
00:02:05.393 --> 00:02:10.373
In the macaque fovea, one red or green sensitive cone feeds its own midget bipolar

30
00:02:10.373 --> 00:02:11.373
cells.

31
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.523
That private centre keeps fine spatial detail.

32
00:02:15.503 --> 00:02:20.343
Midget clusters made up about 85% % of sampled foveal ganglion cells.

33
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:26.253
Shared ancestry with mouse cells does not mean a shared size, frequency or job.

34
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:28.513
Combine the evidence.

35
00:02:29.373 --> 00:02:33.233
A separate mosaic strengthens the case for a type, but it is not required.
